From: Project Luma <maintainers@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] stylesheet: keep the Light title gradient out of Glass

Glass and Frost intentionally ask libadwaita for light foreground semantics.
That makes prefers-color-scheme: light true, but it does not make the selected
surface treatment Light. Scope Filer's deliberate opaque Light gradient to the
actual Light treatment class so the shared AppKit can expose the single
translucent root material in Frost and Glass.

---
 src/resources/style.css | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/resources/style.css b/src/resources/style.css
--- a/src/resources/style.css
+++ b/src/resources/style.css
@@ -22,1 +22,1 @@
-  .luma-files-window headerbar.luma-titlebar {
+  .luma-files-window.luma-treatment-light headerbar.luma-titlebar {
-- 
